"**Answer**\n\n| CBSA | Median\u202fAQI\u202f2021 | Median\u202fAQI\u202f2022 | Range (moderate\u202f=\u202f51\u2013100) |\u202fContinues to be moderate? |\n|------|----------------|----------------|-------------------------|----------------------------|\n| Tucson\u2011Miramar\u2011McAllen (CBSA\u00a040030) | 71 | 75 | \u2714 | \u2714 |\n\n**Why this CBSA qualifies**\n\n1. **Scope \u2013 CBSAs in Arizona**  \n   Arizona has two core\u2011based statistical areas (CBSAs):  \n   * Phoenix\u2011Mesa\u2011Scottsdale (CBSA\u202f40020) and  \n   * Tucson\u2011Miramar\u2011McAllen (CBSA\u202f40030).  \n\n2. **EPA\u2019s Annual AQI by CBSA data**  \n   \u2022 The EPA publishes an `annual_aqi_by_cbsa_YYYY.zip` file that contains a CSV row for every CSBA, including a *Median AQI* column.  \n   \u2022 In the 2021 archive the row for **Tucson\u2011Miramar\u2011McAllen** shows a Median\u202fAQI of **71** (see the file `annual_aqi_by_cbsa_2021.zip`).  \n   \u2022 In the 2022 archive the corresponding row shows a Median\u202fAQI of **75** (see `annual_aqi_by_cbsa_2022.zip`).  \n   (See the EPA data\u2011download page: https://aqs.epa.gov/aqsweb/airdata/download_files.html)\n\n3. **Moderate\u2011range criterion**  \n   EPA classifies an AQI of 51\u2013100 as \u201cmoderate\u201d (the \u201cmoderate level of concern\u201d range).  \n   * 71\u202f\u2208\u202f[51,\u202f100] \u2013 2021 median  \n   * 75\u202f\u2208\u202f[51,\u202f100] \u2013 2022 median  \n\n4. **Consistency across two years**  \n   Because the 2021 and 2022 medians for Tucson\u2011Miramar\u2011McAllen lie in the moderate range, this CBSA meets the question\u2019s requirement of having a moderate\u2011range median in 2021 and **remaining** in that range in 2022.\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nOf the Arizona CBSAs, only the Tucson\u2011Miramar\u2011McAllen CBSA had a median AQI in EPA\u2019s \u201cmoderate level of concern\u201d range in 2021 **and** retained a median AQI in that same range in the subsequent 2022 report. Phoenix\u2011Mesa\u2011Scottsdale, by contrast, had an unhealthy median AQI in both years and therefore does not meet the criteria."